{"title":"KVPY","category":"Engineering","bank":"kvpy","subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","count":13,"questions":[{"id":51981,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let\nWhich of the following statements is FALSE?","options":["$C(0) \\cdot C(\\pi)=1$,","$C(0)+C(\\pi)\\gt 2$","$C(\\theta)\\gt 0$ for all $\\theta \\in R$","$C^{\\prime}(\\theta) \\neq 0$ for all $\\theta \\in R$"],"answer":3,"solution":"\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\mathrm{C}(0)=\\mathrm{e} \\\\\n\\mathrm{C}(\\pi)=\\frac{1}{\\mathrm{e}}\n\\end{array}\n\nOption A, B correct\n\nC^{\\prime}(\\theta)=-\\sum_{\\mathrm{n}-0}^{\\mathrm{x}} \\frac{\\sin \\theta}{(\\mathrm{n}-1) !}\n\nC^{\\prime}(\\theta)=0\n\nOption D false","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21347d18cc920413ff7"},{"id":51982,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of real solutions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></math> is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>","infinite"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>We have,</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHS</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>RHS</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>LHS</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>RHS</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>sec</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>Hence, only one solution.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6a1aec3a3678fdf5158"},{"id":51983,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of solutions of the equation $\\sin \\theta+\\cos \\theta=\\sin 2 \\theta$ in the interval $[-\\pi, \\pi]$ is","options":["1","2","3","4"],"answer":1,"solution":"Squaring $\\sin ^{2} \\theta+\\cos ^{2} \\theta+2 \\sin 2 \\theta=\\sin ^{2} 2 \\theta$\n\\begin{array}{l}\n\\Rightarrow \\sin ^{2} 2 \\theta-\\sin 2 \\theta-1=0 \\\\\n\\sin 2 \\theta=-\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{5}-1}{2}\\right), \\sin 2 \\theta=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}+1}{2}(\\text { reject })\n\\end{array}\n\ntwo solution exist between\n$\\frac{-\\pi}{2}$ to $\\frac{-\\pi}{4} \\& \\frac{\\pi}{4}$ to 0 (2 solution)","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (19 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213bac47ab4aa884a3c"},{"id":51984,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of solutions to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> satisfying <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math> is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>"],"answer":3,"solution":"<p>The given equation </p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>π</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo></math> Integers</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>±</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math>.</p>\n\n<p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>The above equation will hold only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, </p>\n\n<p>so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>k</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo><mo> </mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p>Case <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>II</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>n</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>The above equation will hold only if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>,</p>\n\n<p>so <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>m</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>±</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math>.</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo><mo> </mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> There are total <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math> solutions.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da7279fac8dce0e93b4eb"},{"id":51985,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of real numbers $\\lambda$ for which the equality $\\frac{\\sin (\\lambda \\alpha)}{\\sin \\alpha}-\\frac{\\cos (\\lambda \\alpha)}{\\cos \\alpha}=\\lambda-1$, holds for all real $\\alpha$ which are not integral multiples of $\\pi / 2$ is","options":["1","2","3","Infinite"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\frac{\\sin (\\lambda \\alpha)}{\\sin \\alpha}-\\frac{\\cos (\\lambda \\alpha)}{\\cos \\alpha}=\\lambda-1\\sin \\lambda \\alpha \\cos \\alpha-\\cos \\lambda \\alpha \\sin \\alpha=(\\lambda-1) \\sin \\alpha \\cos \\alpha\\sin (\\lambda \\alpha-\\alpha)=\\frac{(\\lambda-1)}{2} \\sin 2 \\alpha$\nso $=\\lambda=1 ; 3$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2015 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213a16aa89ac4c34e4a"},{"id":51986,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"One of the solutions of the equation $8 \\sin ^{3} \\theta-7 \\sin \\theta+\\sqrt{3} \\cos \\theta=0$ lies in the interval","options":["$\\left(0,10^{\\circ}\\right]$","$\\left(10^{\\circ}, 20^{\\circ}\\right]$","$\\left(20^{\\circ}, 30^{\\circ}\\right]$","$\\left(30^{\\circ}, 40^{\\circ}\\right]$"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\begin{array}{l}\n6 \\sin \\theta-2 \\sin 3 \\theta-7 \\sin \\theta+\\sqrt{3} \\cos \\theta=0 \\\\\n\\sqrt{3} \\cos \\theta-\\sin \\theta=2 \\sin 3 \\theta\n\\end{array}\nIt can be written as\n$\\begin{array}{l}\n2\\left(\\sin \\left(60^{\\circ}-\\theta\\right)\\right)=2 \\sin 3 \\theta \\\\\n\\sin \\left(60^{\\circ}-\\theta\\right)=\\sin 3 \\theta \\\\\n60^{\\circ}=4 \\theta\n\\end{array}\n$\\Rightarrow \\theta=15^{\\circ}$ is one of the value","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (5 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2133cf9c61a12fbcb9c"},{"id":51987,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of solutions of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> in the closed interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>19</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn></math>"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>Given trigonometric equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo></math> either <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math></p>\n\n<p>and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>7</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mi>π</mi></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac></math></p>\n\n<p>So, number of solution of given equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>13</mn></math>.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da7077a81f07f2369fd52"},{"id":51988,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced close=\"}\" open=\"{\"><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>. Then","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is an empty set","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has exactly one point","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has exactly two points","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has more than two points"],"answer":1,"solution":"<p>Given trigonometric relation is </p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>9</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><msup><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>cos</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mi>θ</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>sin</mi><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mn>2</mn><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mo> </mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo> </mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>:</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>π</mi><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"{\" close=\"}\"><mfrac><mi>π</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mi>A</mi><mo>∩</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has exactly one point.</p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2019 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da707e99fd292dbcadcd0"},{"id":51989,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The sum of all $x \\in[0, \\pi]$ which satisfy the equation $\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2} \\cos x=\\sin ^{2}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right)$ is -","options":["$\\frac{\\pi}{6}$","$\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}$","$\\pi$","$2 \\pi$"],"answer":2,"solution":"$\\begin{array}{l}\\sin x+\\frac{1}{2} \\cos x=\\sin ^{2}\\left(x+\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\right) \\\\ \\sin x+\\frac{1}{2} \\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}\\left(1-\\cos \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+2 x\\right)\\right. \\\\ \\sin x+\\frac{1}{2} \\cos x=\\frac{1}{2}(1+\\sin 2 x) \\\\ 2 \\sin x+\\cos x=1+\\sin x \\cos x \\\\ 2 \\sin x \\cos x-2 \\sin x+1-\\cos x=0 \\\\ (1-\\cos x)-2 \\sin x(1-\\cos x)=0 \\\\ (1-\\cos x)(1-2 \\sin x)=0 \\\\ 1-\\cos x=0 & 1-2 \\sin x=0 \\\\ \\cos x=1 \\quad \\sin x=\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ x=0, \\quad x=\\frac{\\pi}{6}, \\frac{5 \\pi}{6} \\\\ \\text { sum }=0+\\frac{\\pi}{6}+\\frac{5 \\pi}{6}=\\pi\\end{array}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2012 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2136001f078d194aafb"},{"id":51990,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of solutions <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> of the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math> in the interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> is","options":["<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn></math>","<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>"],"answer":2,"solution":"<p>Given,</p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>x</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sin</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p>or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>cos</mi><mfenced><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi><mi>π</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>sin</mi><mfrac><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mi>π</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn><mi>π</mi></msqrt></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>±</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>π</mi></msqrt></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math> or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo><</mo><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt><mi>π</mi><mo><</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>π</mi></msqrt><mo>≈</mo><msqrt><mn>25</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>14</mn></msqrt></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>42</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p>\n\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∵</mo></math> Total numbers of solution lies between <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p>","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2018 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"614da6c1761054f04174dddf"},{"id":51991,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of solutions to the equation $\\cos ^{4} x+\\frac{1}{\\cos ^{2} x}=\\sin ^{4} x+\\frac{1}{\\sin ^{2} x}$ in the interval $[0,2 \\pi]$ is :","options":["6","4","2","0"],"answer":1,"solution":"$\\cos ^{4} x-\\sin ^{4} x=\\frac{1}{\\sin ^{2} x}-\\frac{1}{\\cos ^{2} x}\\left(\\cos ^{2} x-\\sin ^{2} x\\right)=\\frac{\\left(\\cos ^{2} x-\\sin ^{2} x\\right)}{\\sin ^{2} x \\cos ^{2} x}\\cos 2 x=\\frac{4 \\cos 2 x}{\\sin ^{2} 2 x}\\cos 2 x\\left(1-4 \\operatorname{cosec}^{2} 2 x\\right)=0\\cos 2 x=02 x=2 n \\pi \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{2}x=n \\pi \\pm \\frac{\\pi}{4}$\nAt $n=0, x=\\frac{\\pi}{4}n=1 ; \\quad x=\\frac{5 \\pi}{4}, \\frac{3 \\pi}{4}n=2, x=\\frac{7 \\pi}{4}$","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2014 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d213673b7ad663261114"},{"id":51992,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"$X=\\{x \\in R: \\cos (\\sin x)=\\sin (\\cos x)\\}$. The number of elements in $X$ is -","options":["0","2","4","not finite"],"answer":0,"solution":"$\\cos (\\sin x)=\\sin (\\cos x)\\sin \\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2} \\pm \\sin x\\right)=\\sin (\\cos x)\\cos x=n \\pi+(-1)^{n}\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}+\\sin x\\right), n \\in I$\n\\Rightarrow \\cos x \\pm \\sin x=n \\pi+(-1)^{\\mathrm{n}} \\frac{\\pi}{2}, \\mathrm{n} \\in \\mathrm{I}\n\nAs LHS $\\in[-\\sqrt{2}, \\sqrt{2}]$, and it does not satisfies RHS So No solution possible","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2016 (SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d21326d4170b215b2165"},{"id":51993,"subject":"Mathematics","chapter":"Trigonometric Equations","exam":"Engineering","examName":"KVPY","q":"The number of real solutions of the equation 2sin $3 x+\\sin 7 x-3=0$ which lie in the interval $[-2 \\pi, 2 \\pi]$ is","options":["1","2","3","4"],"answer":1,"solution":"only possible when $\\sin 3 x=1 \\& \\sin 7 x=1\\sin 3 x=1\\begin{array}{l}\n\\sin 3 x=\\sin (4 n+1) \\frac{\\pi}{2}, n \\in I \\\\\n3 x=(4 n+1) \\frac{\\pi}{2} \\Rightarrow x=(4 n+1) \\frac{\\pi}{6} \\\\\n\\sin 7 x=\\sin (4 m+1) \\frac{\\pi}{2}, m \\in I \\\\\nx=(4 m+1) \\frac{\\pi}{14}\n\\end{array}$\nfor common solution\n$(4 n+1) \\frac{\\pi}{6}=(4 m+1) \\frac{\\pi}{14}$\nSolving these $1=3 \\mathrm{~m}-7 \\mathrm{n}$\nFirst solution is $m=5, n=2$\nSecond solution is $\\mathrm{m}=12, \\mathrm{n}=5$\nSo two solutions are possible","difficulty":"Medium","source":"KVPY 2017 (5 Nov SB/SX)","_marksId":"6174d2136b372920d4b4c3e3"}]}